// EXPECT: E0223 — bitwise operators are integers only (ADR-0042 §5)
// A float's bits are a sign, an exponent and a mantissa, so ANDing two of them produces a
// bit pattern that is not the AND of anything meaningful. A program that wants a float's
// bits will want a cast to an integer of the same width, which Jairs does not have yet.
main :: () {
    a := 1.5;
    b := a & a;
}
